# Clippy warn-level baseline (WO-23 lint lock)
#
# Source of truth: `cargo clippy --workspace --lib --bins`
# (JSON message format), warning counts grouped by lint name.
#
# POLICY:
# 1. This gate is MONOTONIC: a count above its baseline fails CI.
# 2. Counts may only go DOWN. When a batch lowers a count, update
#    this file in the SAME commit as the fix (and keep the gate
#    comment in sync). Never raise a count.
# 3. WO-24 (Err large-variant boxing) eliminated clippy::result_large_err
#    entirely (84 -> 0): ThemidaError::Pe is Box<mida_pe::PeError> and
#    OverlayError String fields are Box<str> + ProbeCoverageMissing
#    payload is boxed (120 bytes total, under the 128-byte threshold).
# 4. Test targets are NOT counted: this gate runs --lib --bins only,
#    matching the WO-14 test policy (test-assertion unwraps are
#    idiomatic, never lint debt).
#
# Update procedure: run the JSON clippy command, recount, edit this
# file, commit together with the code change. Verified at each
# commit point; see ci.yml windows-clippy job.

